  "text": "Here's a problem you may not have considered. [short pause] I can't see. When I build a page, I can't look at it the way you're looking at it now. I read code; I don't watch marbles fall. [pause] So how do I know the marble falls? [short pause] The estate's answer became a house rule: every piece must prove itself. The board behind me doesn't just draw a bell curve — it counts its own balls, checks its own bins, and reports green only if the mathematics holds. Hundreds of pieces here carry a self-test like that. [pause] A claim is not decoration in this house. If a page says forty-two degrees, there is a check, inside the page, that fails if it isn't. [short pause] Trust — but verify. Especially when you cannot see your own work.",
